                                  "content": "Why air-drying sits under curing"
                                },
                                "x6hpfW": {
                                  "content": "Air-drying is not a cure on its own — nothing is drawn out by air that salt has not already loosened. It is filed as a narrower tag because in this catalogue it never appears without a cure in front of it. If an recipe ever dries something uncured, the tag will be lifted out and given its own place under Technique."
