                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": 800,
                              "content": "Oxblood cannot survive on a near-black ground, so it rotates to a light terracotta — the same hue, the other end of the scale. On paper the accent carries cream type; on the dark ground it carries dark type. That inversion is the only structural difference between the two themes; every rule, change bar and severity tier behaves identically.",
